-### [Feed-forward and Generalizable Prediction](15832-feed-forward-and-generalizable-prediction.md)
-Feed-forward and Generalizable Prediction refers to methods that estimate 3D Gaussian Splatting parameters directly from a set of input images in a single forward pass, eliminating the iterative per-scene optimization required by standard 3D Gaussian Splatting. This family solves the problem of slow reconstruction and the dependency on Structure-from-Motion (SfM) preprocessing by leveraging learned priors from large-scale datasets. What sets this approach apart from iterative inverse rendering is the shift from optimization-based recovery to regression-based prediction, enabling real-time or near-real-time novel view synthesis and reconstruction.
